{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":29,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b1","text":"Page 29","bbox":[343.84,587.64,369.0,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b2","text":"d20 Feature Condition","bbox":[53.69,75.0,314.9,86.08]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b3","text":"1 Abandoned Fields Bandit Ambushes","bbox":[59.13,93.85,328.04,104.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b4","text":"2 Blood-Red Blocked by Giant Boulder","bbox":[58.62,110.05,343.03,121.13]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b5","text":"3 Buried Charms Collapsed Bridge","bbox":[58.51,126.25,327.22,137.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b6","text":"4 Cattle Prints Confusing to Navigate","bbox":[58.56,142.45,337.04,153.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b7","text":"5 Constant Patrols Dense Bramble","bbox":[58.59,158.65,323.97,169.73]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b8","text":"6 Dead Vegetation Divided by Political Dispute","bbox":[58.45,174.85,347.05,185.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b9","text":"7 Disappearing Erratic Weather","bbox":[58.87,191.05,325.8,202.13]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b10","text":"8 Diseased Animals Frequent Flash Floods","bbox":[58.46,207.25,336.7,218.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b11","text":"9 Follows the Stars Gets Extremely Cold","bbox":[58.45,223.45,334.21,234.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b12","text":"10 Frequent Pilgrims Heavy Toll Required","bbox":[56.58,239.65,333.33,250.73]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b13","text":"11 Massive Grooves Labyrinthine Canyons","bbox":[57.5,255.85,336.71,266.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b14","text":"12 Mile Markers Night Predators","bbox":[56.99,272.05,325.51,283.13]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b15","text":"13 Mineral Flecks Occasional Stampedes","bbox":[56.89,288.25,337.74,299.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b16","text":"14 Newly Made Overcrowded","bbox":[56.94,304.45,321.33,315.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b17","text":"15 Overgrown Passes over Rapids","bbox":[56.97,320.65,330.78,331.73]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b18","text":"16 Rusted Tools Poisonous Fruit","bbox":[56.83,336.85,325.0,347.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b19","text":"17 Shredded Smoke-filled","bbox":[57.25,353.05,319.56,364.13]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b20","text":"18 Shriveled Away Steep Climb","bbox":[56.84,369.25,318.38,380.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b21","text":"19 Twisted Thick Evening Mist","bbox":[56.82,385.45,331.4,396.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b22","text":"20 Ubiquitous Footprints Uneven, Soggy Ground","bbox":[56.07,401.65,338.68,412.73]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b23","text":"PATH FEATURES","bbox":[45.0,44.14,110.66,55.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b24","text":"Roll 1d20 for each column and combine.","bbox":[45.0,56.25,174.34,65.94]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b25","text":"Terrain Difficulty","bbox":[173.27,426.74,240.73,437.82]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b26","text":"Difficulty Terrain Penalty Factors","bbox":[49.5,446.97,261.56,458.05]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b27","text":"Easy Plains, plateaus, valleys None Safe areas for rest, fellow travelers, good visibility.","bbox":[49.5,464.49,365.91,486.57]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b28","text":"Tough Forests, deserts, hills +1 Watch","bbox":[49.5,498.04,213.31,520.12]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b29","text":"Wild animals, flooding, broken equipment, falling rocks, unsafe shelters, hunter’s traps","bbox":[233.1,492.54,353.36,525.62]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b30","text":"Perilous Mountains, jungles, swamps +2 Watches","bbox":[49.5,537.09,222.73,559.17]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-29-b31","text":"Quicksand, sucking mud, choking vines, unclean water, poisonous plants and animals, poor navigation","bbox":[233.1,531.59,364.5,564.67]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-29-b23","a-cairn-warden-29-b24","a-cairn-warden-29-b2","a-cairn-warden-29-b3","a-cairn-warden-29-b4","a-cairn-warden-29-b5","a-cairn-warden-29-b6","a-cairn-warden-29-b7","a-cairn-warden-29-b8","a-cairn-warden-29-b9","a-cairn-warden-29-b10","a-cairn-warden-29-b11","a-cairn-warden-29-b12","a-cairn-warden-29-b13","a-cairn-warden-29-b14","a-cairn-warden-29-b15","a-cairn-warden-29-b16","a-cairn-warden-29-b17","a-cairn-warden-29-b18","a-cairn-warden-29-b19","a-cairn-warden-29-b20","a-cairn-warden-29-b21","a-cairn-warden-29-b22","a-cairn-warden-29-b25","a-cairn-warden-29-b26","a-cairn-warden-29-b27","a-cairn-warden-29-b29","a-cairn-warden-29-b28","a-cairn-warden-29-b31","a-cairn-warden-29-b30","a-cairn-warden-29-b1"],"headings":[]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":32,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b1","text":"Page 32","bbox":[27.0,587.64,52.02,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b2","text":"Dungeon Seeds","bbox":[27.0,42.84,173.56,70.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b3","text":"Dungeon Principles","bbox":[27.0,79.65,140.23,96.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b4","text":"Purpose Consider what the dungeon’s original purpose was as well as what it is being used for today. Demonstrate a dungeon’s history by including signs of its original inhabitants and their goals. Sometimes a dungeon will have multiple purposes, and these can collide against each other to create tension among its denizens.","bbox":[27.0,102.88,345.21,160.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b5","text":"Levels Though they should make sense as part of the dungeon’s construction and purpose, levels should also represent increasing danger. On each level, try to push players to weigh the risk of further exploration versus a potential reward.","bbox":[27.0,167.88,340.13,214.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b6","text":"Layout Create multiple entrances and exits, offer multiple routes, design choke points, and provide hiding spots. Add meaningful and obvious information to room entrances and exits.","bbox":[27.0,221.88,347.3,268.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b7","text":"Verticality Incorporate tall rooms, climbable structures, and paths that allow movement around and over obstacles.","bbox":[27.0,275.88,343.6,311.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b8","text":"Secret Areas Include hidden zones, including at least one that will likely remain undiscovered but is still worth finding. Try to avoid hiding crucial information behind secret rooms.","bbox":[27.0,318.88,349.47,354.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b9","text":"Rooms Vary room shapes, sizes, and functions. Use architectural motifs to connect rooms and provide hints of what’s to come. Room descriptions should be easy to map and recall.","bbox":[27.0,361.88,351.26,397.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b10","text":"Treasure Incorporate a variety of treasures beyond mere gold, such as knowledge, allies, trade goods, and artifacts. Add narrative elements to treasure to increase its non-monetary value.","bbox":[27.0,404.88,346.9,451.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b11","text":"Challenges Allow the characters to drive the story by writing challenges without prescribed outcomes. Create a sense of peril, but avoid making obstacles seem unbeatable. Overly dangerous areas and creatures should be obvious. Create encounters that can be avoided with critical thinking and problem-solving, not just violence. Remember that monsters and other obstacles are another way to tell the dungeon’s story.","bbox":[27.0,458.88,350.9,527.19]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-32-b2","a-cairn-warden-32-b3","a-cairn-warden-32-b4","a-cairn-warden-32-b5","a-cairn-warden-32-b6","a-cairn-warden-32-b7","a-cairn-warden-32-b8","a-cairn-warden-32-b9","a-cairn-warden-32-b10","a-cairn-warden-32-b11","a-cairn-warden-32-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b2","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b3","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-3","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b5","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-4","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b5","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-5","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b6","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-6","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b7","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-7","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b8","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-8","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b7","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-9","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b10","level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-10","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b11","level":3}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":33,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b1","text":"Page 33","bbox":[343.84,587.64,369.0,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b2","text":"NPCs Include engaging NPCs with their own goals and agendas. These characters may want to stay in the dungeon; they may even love it! NPCs and monsters should communicate with the PCs, even during combat. Have them make threats, suggest compromises, or try to persuade the PCs whenever possible. Every character wants something, and has a limit to what they might do to get it.","bbox":[45.0,43.92,370.7,112.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b3","text":"Factions Factions should interact with both the characters and one another, acting on their own regardless of the character’s actions. Give them hierarchies and divisions that can be exploited.","bbox":[45.0,119.92,368.86,166.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b4","text":"Puzzles Create puzzles that have clear, actionable goals. Puzzles should reinforce the themes of the dungeon and build on its history. Make the challenge of the puzzle obvious, but the solution less so. Allow for multiple solutions, and for players to solve them using intelligence and critical thinking, not just special abilities or tools. Create built-in clues suggesting the puzzle’s origin and its effects.","bbox":[45.0,173.92,369.55,242.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b5","text":"The Dungeon Map Put boring or repetitive stuff (exits, room shapes, etc.) on the map, rather than in the room description. Obvious exits should be described using clear, distinct language. Number your rooms to help avoid confusion when referencing the map.","bbox":[45.0,249.92,361.76,296.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b6","text":"Room Keying Emphasize a room’s most important aspects (typically obvious threats or NPCs). Describe elements that help orient the party to their surroundings. Be specific, but avoid describing how the characters should feel. Only describe what’s happening now. If there is history here, the characters will discover it in play. Name each room!","bbox":[45.0,303.92,367.28,361.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b7","text":"Encounter Tables Create random events to help make a dungeon feel alive by making exploration tense and unpredictable, as parties may encounter wandering monsters, factions, NPCs, or signs of an approaching threat. Try to provide challenges, moments of respite, or opportunities for roleplay.","bbox":[45.0,368.92,362.92,426.23]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-33-b2","a-cairn-warden-33-b3","a-cairn-warden-33-b4","a-cairn-warden-33-b5","a-cairn-warden-33-b6","a-cairn-warden-33-b7","a-cairn-warden-33-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b7","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-2","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b3","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-3","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b4","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-4","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b5","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-5","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b6","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-6","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b7","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":56,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b1","text":"Page 56","bbox":[27.0,587.64,52.22,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b2","text":"Forest Seeds","bbox":[27.0,42.84,148.42,70.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b3","text":"Forestcrawls","bbox":[27.0,79.65,101.2,96.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b4","text":"A forestcrawl is a simple method for exploring a large forested area, typically made up of branching trails connecting scattered points of interest. While a forestcrawl has some of the same properties as a traditional dungeon delve, it swaps stone walls and ceilings for the dense, non-linear design of a heavily wooded area. Instead of rooms, points of interest are defined as clearings or major changes in the forested landscape. However unlike exploring a dungeon, characters can take shortcuts, go “off-trail,” or climb trees to get a better look around (with a cost, of course).","bbox":[27.0,99.61,347.46,176.69]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b5","text":"Exploring The Wood","bbox":[27.0,184.38,124.3,198.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b6","text":"• Follow the Dungeon Exploration procedures found in the Player’s Guide, but rather than rolling for Dungeon Events, use the Wilderness Events table instead.","bbox":[31.5,202.11,351.72,224.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b7","text":"• If the party attempts to step off the trail and cut through the forest, the Warden should make any associated costs clear: added travel time, effort, special tools that may be required, and any obvious dangers. Going off-trail also automatically triggers a roll on the Wilderness Events table.","bbox":[31.5,228.61,343.18,272.69]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b8","text":"• Points in a forestcrawl are close to each other. When traveling on clearly marked trails, a small forest (10-15 POIs) can be explored in a single Watch.","bbox":[31.5,277.11,342.91,299.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b9","text":"• Rely on the fiction and common sense to determine how much daylight is available, whether a suitable area is available for rest, and what the costs or dangers the forest may contain in the darkness.","bbox":[31.5,303.61,352.18,336.69]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b10","text":"Creating a Forest","bbox":[27.0,344.55,126.19,361.17]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b11","text":"Follow this procedure for any forested terrain in a region. If a conflict or interesting pattern emerges, be open to restating or modifying any earlier results!","bbox":[27.0,364.51,340.54,386.59]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b12","text":"Materials Required","bbox":[39.0,445.52,130.94,459.37]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b13","text":"• A sheet of paper and a notebook. Letter/A4 is fine.","bbox":[40.5,463.25,173.51,485.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b14","text":"• Pencils and erasers. Colored pencils or crayons are good, too.","bbox":[40.5,489.75,185.38,511.83]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b15","text":"• At least one d6 and one d20, but 6d6 and 2d20 would be ideal.","bbox":[40.5,516.25,171.4,538.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b16","text":"Overview","bbox":[193.5,445.52,238.89,459.37]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b17","text":"1. Describe the forest.","bbox":[196.2,463.25,280.34,474.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b18","text":"2. Describe the spirit of the forest.","bbox":[196.2,478.75,325.8,489.83]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b19","text":"3. Create the forests’s POIs.","bbox":[196.2,494.25,300.82,505.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b20","text":"4. Create the forests’s trails.","bbox":[196.2,509.75,302.06,520.83]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b21","text":"5. Create forest encounters.","bbox":[196.2,525.25,302.47,536.33]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b22","text":"6. Name the forest.","bbox":[196.2,540.75,269.1,551.83]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b23","text":"Going forward, we will refer to the sheet of paper as the map. As with any other rule, if you don’t like a table result, roll again or tweak as desired!","bbox":[40.5,406.72,340.25,426.97]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-56-b2","a-cairn-warden-56-b3","a-cairn-warden-56-b4","a-cairn-warden-56-b5","a-cairn-warden-56-b6","a-cairn-warden-56-b7","a-cairn-warden-56-b8","a-cairn-warden-56-b9","a-cairn-warden-56-b10","a-cairn-warden-56-b11","a-cairn-warden-56-b23","a-cairn-warden-56-b12","a-cairn-warden-56-b16","a-cairn-warden-56-b13","a-cairn-warden-56-b17","a-cairn-warden-56-b18","a-cairn-warden-56-b14","a-cairn-warden-56-b19","a-cairn-warden-56-b20","a-cairn-warden-56-b15","a-cairn-warden-56-b21","a-cairn-warden-56-b22","a-cairn-warden-56-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-56-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b2","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-56-2","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b3","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-56-3","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b5","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-56-4","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-56-b10","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":68,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b1","text":"Page 68","bbox":[27.0,587.64,52.34,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b2","text":"Example Forest","bbox":[27.0,42.84,174.66,70.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b3","text":"1. Diseased Campsite (E)","bbox":[215.96,267.76,295.7,277.46]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b4","text":"Old Logging Road","bbox":[123.04,297.76,180.63,307.46]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b5","text":"Foraging Path","bbox":[123.04,311.08,168.17,320.78]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b6","text":"Hunter’s Track","bbox":[123.04,324.4,171.37,334.1]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b7","text":"Treeline Heights","bbox":[289.83,296.6,343.92,306.3]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b8","text":"Dry Riverbed","bbox":[289.83,309.92,332.39,319.62]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b9","text":"Hidden","bbox":[289.83,322.52,313.67,332.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b10","text":"4. Anglwyst’s Chicken Hut","bbox":[269.24,96.58,314.17,116.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b11","text":"3. Sweeney’s Cabin","bbox":[249.8,152.32,293.37,172.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b12","text":"8. Black Mass","bbox":[53.66,196.96,98.5,206.66]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b13","text":"9. Fishing Hut","bbox":[55.4,99.04,102.28,108.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b14","text":"2. Amber Grave","bbox":[267.08,214.96,318.21,224.66]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b15","text":"7. Flooded Abbey","bbox":[73.4,266.2,128.53,275.9]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b16","text":"5. Tree at the Crossroads","bbox":[167.0,203.68,212.78,223.38]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b17","text":"6. Gray Sanctuary","bbox":[126.5,148.0,186.04,157.7]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b18","text":"The Forest","bbox":[27.0,357.98,88.5,374.6]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b19","text":"DESCRIPTION Diseased, Frozen","bbox":[27.0,377.94,90.14,400.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b20","text":"• A thick forest infected with disease and rot. Parts of it are frozen solid.","bbox":[31.5,404.44,302.49,415.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b21","text":"DENIZENS Traits: Stable, Territorial","bbox":[27.0,419.94,119.62,442.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b22","text":"• Wish to return to the stability they once knew, but are threatened by ancient forest boundaries.","bbox":[31.5,446.44,352.92,468.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b23","text":"FOREST AGENDA Traits: Purification, Infestation","bbox":[27.0,472.94,142.23,495.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b24","text":"• The spirit of the forest wants nothing more than to purify itself of the disease that has taken hold. An infestation of Giant Spiders (9) has spun webs throughout, killing far too many creatures and undermining the ecosystem.","bbox":[31.5,499.44,346.21,532.52]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-68-b2","a-cairn-warden-68-b10","a-cairn-warden-68-b13","a-cairn-warden-68-b17","a-cairn-warden-68-b11","a-cairn-warden-68-b12","a-cairn-warden-68-b16","a-cairn-warden-68-b14","a-cairn-warden-68-b15","a-cairn-warden-68-b3","a-cairn-warden-68-b7","a-cairn-warden-68-b4","a-cairn-warden-68-b8","a-cairn-warden-68-b5","a-cairn-warden-68-b9","a-cairn-warden-68-b6","a-cairn-warden-68-b18","a-cairn-warden-68-b19","a-cairn-warden-68-b20","a-cairn-warden-68-b21","a-cairn-warden-68-b22","a-cairn-warden-68-b23","a-cairn-warden-68-b24","a-cairn-warden-68-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-68-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b2","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-68-2","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-68-b18","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":102,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b1","text":"Page 102","bbox":[27.0,587.64,55.01,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b2","text":"Unicorn","bbox":[34.45,170.89,73.68,184.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b3","text":"6 HP, 14 STR, 12 DEX, 14 WIL, horn (d10, ignores armor)","bbox":[34.45,188.73,163.55,208.43]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b4","text":"• Magical horses with a single long horn on their foreheads. Timid, but proud and willful, are seen as divine beings.","bbox":[38.95,213.23,174.35,242.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b5","text":"• Their hair is worth a small fortune due to its powerful healing properties.","bbox":[38.95,245.57,174.9,265.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b6","text":"Troll","bbox":[34.45,53.17,57.65,67.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b7","text":"14 HP, 1 Armor, 14 STR, 12 DEX, 4 WIL, claw (d8), club (d10)","bbox":[34.45,71.01,221.62,80.71]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b8","text":"• Giant, warty humanoids of flesh and bark. Dwell underground or in deep forests, as well as the ruined homes of their former victims. Carnivorous.","bbox":[38.95,85.51,344.0,105.21]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b9","text":"• When taking critical damage, a Troll will continue fighting, despite loss of flesh and limb. Only when their STR is 0 are they truly killed. Unless their heads are bathed in acid, fire, or powerful magic, they will fully regenerate within 1d4 days.","bbox":[38.95,107.85,344.83,137.55]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b10","text":"Viper","bbox":[200.95,170.89,227.49,184.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b11","text":"3 HP, 5 STR, 12 DEX, 3 WIL, bite (d6)","bbox":[200.95,188.73,317.58,198.43]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b12","text":"• Poisonous snakes often found in caves, pits, and other dark places. An antitoxin can be made from their poison sacs.","bbox":[205.45,203.23,333.98,242.93]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b13","text":"• Use heat and smell to track their victims.","bbox":[205.45,245.57,322.43,265.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b14","text":"• Critical Damage: Target is poisoned, dying in 1d12 hours without a cure.","bbox":[205.45,267.91,335.56,287.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b15","text":"Warp Panther","bbox":[34.45,313.45,101.8,327.3]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b16","text":"8 HP, 13 STR, 16 DEX, 12 WIL, tentacles (d8+d8, blast ), bite (d10)","bbox":[34.45,331.29,237.25,341.08]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b17","text":"• Grotesque panther-like predators with long razored tentacles growing out of their backs.","bbox":[38.95,345.79,338.51,355.49]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b18","text":"• Resistant to magical attacks. Caster must make a WIL save for the intended effect to succeed.","bbox":[38.95,358.13,323.44,377.83]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b19","text":"• Can teleport a short distance away at will. Hate Blink Dogs.","bbox":[38.95,380.47,239.6,390.17]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-102-b6","a-cairn-warden-102-b7","a-cairn-warden-102-b8","a-cairn-warden-102-b9","a-cairn-warden-102-b2","a-cairn-warden-102-b10","a-cairn-warden-102-b3","a-cairn-warden-102-b11","a-cairn-warden-102-b12","a-cairn-warden-102-b4","a-cairn-warden-102-b5","a-cairn-warden-102-b13","a-cairn-warden-102-b14","a-cairn-warden-102-b15","a-cairn-warden-102-b16","a-cairn-warden-102-b17","a-cairn-warden-102-b18","a-cairn-warden-102-b19","a-cairn-warden-102-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-102-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b6","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-102-2","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b2","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-102-3","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b10","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-102-4","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-102-b15","level":2}]}
