{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":130,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-130-b1","text":"Page 130","bbox":[27.0,587.64,55.15,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-130-b2","text":"LEARNING THROUGH TRIAL AND ERROR","bbox":[145.44,44.14,307.04,55.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-130-b3","text":"Julius was bookish, nervous, and not particularly strong or dexterous. Over months of adventuring, he had developed a strategy to avoid direct confrontation in combat, which involved throwing a weighted net onto an opponent. While the target was prone and defenseless, Julius, without adequate protection from his allies, would be at high risk, especially when facing multiple opponents. Each time Julius attempted this, his player would need to explain exactly how he approached his target, and if the obvious risks weren’t mitigated, the Warden would require a DEX save to succeed. After a particularly risky attempt failed, all of the players (including the Warden) were so impressed by the care and strategy that went into the attempt that the Warden ruled that going forward, Julius would no longer need to make a save when throwing the net in combat. Instead, it would succeed automatically, as Julius had clearly learned how to capture targets in his net safely.","bbox":[145.44,59.64,351.66,268.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-130-b4","text":"Warden Notes","bbox":[37.0,53.14,91.62,64.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-130-b5","text":"In this example, we can see that although Julius had occasionally failed in his repeated attempts to avoid direct combat by employing a unique battle strategy, the thought and preparation that went into each attempt coupled with the character’s insistence to “get it right” were sufficient to grant that character a new ability. Remember that in a typical combat scenario, the PCs have already rolled DEX saves at the beginning of combat, so future DEX saves are really only required when a character puts themselves at further risk through an act of bravery, tries to flee combat, etc. A save isn’t necessarily required from the target of an action either, as only the character most at risk saves.","bbox":[36.0,69.19,124.19,420.58]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-130-b2","a-cairn-warden-130-b4","a-cairn-warden-130-b3","a-cairn-warden-130-b5","a-cairn-warden-130-b1"],"headings":[]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":165,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b1","text":"Page 165","bbox":[341.23,587.64,369.0,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b2","text":"down from the ceiling. If it closes, you’ll be locked in this section of the jail! Wolfram, you can probably make it through without any risk. Lucius and Freya will need to each make DEX saves in order to make it.”","bbox":[49.5,44.14,366.07,77.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b3","text":"Wolfram: “I’m going to stop and hold the gate for as long as I can. What do I risk?”","bbox":[45.0,81.64,348.82,92.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b4","text":"Warden: “The gate is strong. It might break your bones, or you might get stuck","bbox":[45.0,97.14,339.74,108.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b5","text":"underneath.”","bbox":[49.5,108.14,97.68,119.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b6","text":"Wolfram: “I toss the bundle through to the other side, then take up a position to grab","bbox":[45.0,123.64,363.98,134.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b7","text":"onto it. Lucius, Freya, you two run ahead. I’ve got this.”","bbox":[49.5,134.64,252.48,145.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b8","text":"Lucius and Freya agree, and Wolfram rolls a 13: a success!","bbox":[58.5,154.3,255.67,164.55]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b9","text":"Warden: “You groan as the iron bars press down against your arms and shoulders. Just","bbox":[45.0,173.64,369.02,184.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b10","text":"as you feel like the gate might crush you in two, Lucius and Freya jog past and into safety. You step back and the gate collapses onto the stone floor with such force that the mechanism itself breaks. There is no going back now! The large guard isn’t getting through either, though.”","bbox":[49.5,184.64,370.43,228.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b11","text":"Wolfram: “It’s just as I’ve always said: ‘Through strength, there is virtue.’ Or was it,","bbox":[45.0,233.14,352.06,244.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b12","text":"‘There is virtue in strength?’ Ah, anyway… Hey, wait for me!”","bbox":[49.5,244.14,272.39,255.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b13","text":"DEXTERITY","bbox":[45.0,264.14,90.97,275.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b14","text":"Freya crouches atop the rafters of a decrepit tavern, spying on a gang of heavily-armed thugs below.","bbox":[58.5,279.3,359.81,299.55]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b15","text":"Warden: “After twenty minutes of cramped discomfort, the care and caution you","bbox":[45.0,308.64,347.53,319.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b16","text":"put into this venture are finally rewarded as one of the men below speaks aloud the location of their hideout. Your mission is complete! What do you do now?”","bbox":[49.5,319.64,361.24,341.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b17","text":"Freya: “I need to skedaddle without these jokers knowing I was ever here. Does it look","bbox":[45.0,346.14,366.82,357.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b18","text":"like they are nearly finished?”","bbox":[49.5,357.14,158.82,368.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b19","text":"Warden: “Actually, one of them is pulling out a deck of cards, and the others are","bbox":[45.0,372.64,344.15,383.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b20","text":"nodding in approval. It looks like they’ll be here for a while yet.”","bbox":[49.5,383.64,284.45,394.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b21","text":"Freya: “Rats. Well, no time like the present, right? I’m going to sneak back the way I","bbox":[45.0,399.14,355.88,410.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b22","text":"came.”","bbox":[49.5,410.14,74.13,421.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b23","text":"Warden: “That’s fine, but when you passed earlier there was no one here. That is no","bbox":[45.0,425.64,357.99,436.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b24","text":"longer the case! You’ll need to make a DEX save to avoid detection.”","bbox":[49.5,436.64,300.3,447.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b25","text":"Freya rolls a 16: a fail!","bbox":[58.5,456.3,131.05,466.55]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b26","text":"Warden: “As you crest the final beam, it creaks. All six of the men look up and see you","bbox":[45.0,475.64,364.62,486.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b27","text":"leap into the crawlspace leading out of the main hall and into the kitchens. They didn’t get a bead on your face, but they know you’re up there! They shout and draw their weapons.”","bbox":[49.5,486.64,360.31,519.72]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b28","text":"Freya: “I have one smoke bomb left, and I plan on using it. I’m going to drop into the","bbox":[45.0,524.14,358.66,535.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b29","text":"kitchens to find a pot. If I recall correctly, water makes the smoke go crazy…“","bbox":[49.5,535.14,336.36,546.22]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b30","text":"Advice and Examples: Frequently Asked Questions","bbox":[202.72,14.36,369.0,24.06]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-165-b30","a-cairn-warden-165-b2","a-cairn-warden-165-b3","a-cairn-warden-165-b4","a-cairn-warden-165-b5","a-cairn-warden-165-b6","a-cairn-warden-165-b7","a-cairn-warden-165-b8","a-cairn-warden-165-b9","a-cairn-warden-165-b10","a-cairn-warden-165-b11","a-cairn-warden-165-b12","a-cairn-warden-165-b13","a-cairn-warden-165-b14","a-cairn-warden-165-b15","a-cairn-warden-165-b16","a-cairn-warden-165-b17","a-cairn-warden-165-b18","a-cairn-warden-165-b19","a-cairn-warden-165-b20","a-cairn-warden-165-b21","a-cairn-warden-165-b22","a-cairn-warden-165-b23","a-cairn-warden-165-b24","a-cairn-warden-165-b25","a-cairn-warden-165-b26","a-cairn-warden-165-b27","a-cairn-warden-165-b28","a-cairn-warden-165-b29","a-cairn-warden-165-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-165-1","block_id":"a-cairn-warden-165-b13","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":177,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b1","text":"Page 177","bbox":[342.64,587.64,369.0,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b2","text":"Wolfram rolls a d6, dealing 2 damage to the shorter man, who has enough HP to absorb the attack. Freya rolls a d6 for each of her daggers, dealing a 1 and a 3. She keeps only the higher die, and the large man is able to absorb the damage, taking his HP down to 0 (but only PCs gain Scars). Lucius rolls a 6 against the woman [5 HP, 11 STR, 8 DEX, 14 WIL]. She loses 1 point of STR in the attack and so must then roll a Critical Damage save using her new STR score.","bbox":[58.5,44.2,367.65,104.45]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b3","text":"Warden: “Wolfram, you stab at the shorter man, but he deftly avoids your attack!","bbox":[45.0,113.53,347.5,124.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b4","text":"Freya, your daggers slice at the large man with impressive speed and intensity, and it’s clear that you’ve put him on the defensive, as you can see the sweat begin pouring down the sides of his head. He is running out of steam! Lucius, your cane sword pierces the woman in the stomach! She makes a STR save to see if she can stay in the fight. She rolls a 13, a fail! She goes down!”","bbox":[49.5,124.53,369.36,179.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b5","text":"This is the first casualty of the fight, so the woman’s allies must make a WIL save to continue or flee. The Warden rolls using the leader’s WIL, and he fails!","bbox":[58.5,188.2,345.52,208.45]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b6","text":"Warden: “The short man sees his sister fall and screams a cry of anguish. He drops his","bbox":[45.0,217.53,366.56,228.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b7","text":"sword and commands the larger man to drop his ax. ‘Please,’ he begs. ‘I don’t care about whatever is in that barrow. I beg of you: have mercy. Save my sister, if you have the means.’“","bbox":[49.5,228.53,369.02,261.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b8","text":"Wolfram: “My order takes mercy on all folk willing to forge a new path. If we save your","bbox":[45.0,266.03,368.62,277.11]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b9","text":"sister with our skills and resources, will you vow to pledge yourself to a life of piety, poverty, and kindness?”","bbox":[49.5,277.03,362.04,299.11]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b10","text":"Warden: “The shorter man nods, then rushes to his sister. The larger man only smiles,","bbox":[45.0,303.53,366.6,314.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b11","text":"then says, ‘I ain’t swearin’ nothin’. But I do what he says, so long as he pays. Just let me keep my ax.’“","bbox":[49.5,314.53,357.73,336.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b12","text":"The party bandage up the woman, stabilizing her. Had they not, she would have bled out within the hour. Now out of danger, the PCs take a quick swig of water and regain their lost HP. Lucius tries to impress Freya by showing off the new battle scar on his eyebrow, but it doesn’t work.","bbox":[58.5,345.2,364.45,385.45]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b13","text":"Wolfram: “Alright, that’s all sorted then. You lot make your way back to town, and we’ll","bbox":[45.0,394.53,369.12,405.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b14","text":"convene later. For now, we’ve got business with this Cutlass King I’ve read so much about.”","bbox":[49.5,405.53,359.85,427.61]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-177-b15","text":"Advice and Examples: Frequently Asked Questions","bbox":[202.72,14.36,369.0,24.06]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-177-b15","a-cairn-warden-177-b2","a-cairn-warden-177-b3","a-cairn-warden-177-b4","a-cairn-warden-177-b5","a-cairn-warden-177-b6","a-cairn-warden-177-b7","a-cairn-warden-177-b8","a-cairn-warden-177-b9","a-cairn-warden-177-b10","a-cairn-warden-177-b11","a-cairn-warden-177-b12","a-cairn-warden-177-b13","a-cairn-warden-177-b14","a-cairn-warden-177-b1"],"headings":[]}
